2.1.2 Percentage distribution of population by LGA
The total population of The Gambia was 1,857,181 in 2013, of which 49.2 per cent were
males and 50.8 per cent were females. With the exception of Banjul and Kanifing LGAs, the
other LGAs have relatively more females than males. Brikama LGA is the only LGA which
had equal proportion of both sexes (Table 2.1.2 below).
