2.1.3 Distribution of the population by sex and residence
In general, the rural areas had more females (51.9 per cent) compared to males (48.1 per
cent). This can be attributed to migration which is both sex and age selective. However, the
equal proportion of males and females in the urban population was more of urban
reclassification of settlements than migration (Table 2.1.3 below). Most of the urban
reclassification occurred in the Brikama LGA, where the proportion of males and females
were the same (Table 2.1.2 above).
