3.2 Population distribution by ethnicity and LGA
All the ethnic groups were found in each of the LGAs, although their proportions differ. The
Mandinkas are found in large numbers in the Kanifing, Brikama and Mansakonko LGAs
while the Fulas form the majority in the Kuntaur and Janjanbureh LGAs. The Wollofs
constitute the majority in the Banjul and Kerewan LGAs and the Jolas are found mainly in
the Kanifing and Brikama LGAs. The Sarahules are predominantly found in the Basse LGA
while the Sereres and Creole/Aku Marabou are predominantly found in Banjul (Table 3.2
below).
