3.3.1 Non-Gambian population
The non-Gambian population has doubled in size during the 1983–1993 inter-censal period.
From 1993 to 2013, the non-Gambian population has declined from 134,118 in 1993 to
114,968 in 2003 and to 110,705 in 2013. This decline could be partly attributed to returning
home and re-settlement of large number of refugees from the then conflict ridden countries in
the sub-region such as Sierra Leone and Liberia (refer to annex, Table B.5).
3.3.2 Distribution of the population by nationality and LGA
The Gambians form the majority in all the LGAs representing 94.0 per cent of the total
population (refer to annex, Table B.4). The non-Africans are largely concentrated in Banjul,
Kanifing and Brikama LGAs. The Senegalese constituted the majority of non-nationals with
44.3 per cent (refer to annex, Table C.1) of the total enumerated population in 2013.
