3.3.3 Distribution of non-Gambians by nationality
The proportion of Guinea-Bissau nationals in The Gambia has been declining over the last
three decades, from 9.3 per cent in 1983 to 6.3 per cent in 1993 and further declined to 4.8
per cent in 2003 followed by an upsurge of 5.5 per cent in 2013. The steep declines in the
last three decades (1983-2003) could be attributed to the return of the refugees following the
end of the war for independence with the Portuguese, which culminated in Guinea-Bissau’s
independence in 1974. The slight upsurge in the 2013 proportion of Guinea-Bissau nationals
might be the result of the series of unrest and frequent changes of government experienced by
Guinea-Bissau which ushered in a period of political and economic instability up until 2013
(refer to annex, Table C.1).
